        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1504a269-c395-5d7f-a111-f6de89a358ef",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kyosuke Himuro, Boy George, Yukinojo Mori, Shou Tajima\n- Organizations: Boøwy\n- Works: \"Do You Really Want to Hurt Me\", \"Time (Clock of the Heart)\", \"Karma Chameleon\", \"Dragon Ball Z\"\n- Places: Takasaki, Gunma, Japan, Saitama, Japan\n- Roles: singer-songwriter, musician, lead vocalist, DJ, fashion designer, photographer, manga illustrator, anime character designer, songwriter\n\nFacts:\n- Kyosuke Himuro was born on October 7, 1960, in Takasaki, Gunma, Japan.\n- Boy George was born as George Alan O'Dowd on June 14, 1961.\n- Shou Tajima was born on February 7, 1966, in Saitama, Japan.\n- Kyosuke Himuro is a Japanese singer-songwriter and musician.\n- From 1981 to 1988, Kyosuke Himuro was the lead vocalist of the rock band Boøwy.\n- During the 1980s, Boy George's band recorded global hit songs including \"Do You Really Want to Hurt Me\", \"Time (Clock of the Heart)\", and \"Karma Chameleon\".\n- Boy George is an English singer, songwriter, DJ, fashion designer, and photographer known for his soulful voice and androgynous appearance.\n- Yukinojo Mori has written over 2,000 songs for artists including Kyosuke Himuro, Takuro Yoshida, and Junichi Inagaki.\n- Yukinojo Mori has also written theme songs for anime series including \"Dragon Ball Z\".\n- Shou Tajima is a manga illustrator and anime character designer.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "59c1b983-0c95-5954-b40b-7a3eaead0815",
        "text": "Page: Kyosuke Himuro. Sentence: Kyosuke Himuro (氷室 京介 , Himuro Kyōsuke , born October 7, 1960 in Takasaki, Gunma, Japan) is a Japanese singer-songwriter and musician.\nPage: Kyosuke Himuro. Sentence: He was a lead vocalist of the rock band Boøwy from 1981 to 1988.\nPage: Boy George. Sentence: Boy George (born George Alan O'Dowd; 14 June 1961) is an English singer, songwriter, DJ, fashion designer and photographer.\nPage: Boy George. Sentence: At the height of the band's fame, during the 1980s, they recorded global hit songs such as \"Do You Really Want to Hurt Me\", \"Time (Clock of the Heart)\" and \"Karma Chameleon\" and George is known for his soulful voice and androgynous appearance.\nPage: Yukinojo Mori. Sentence: He has written over 2,000 songs for numerous artists such as Kyosuke Himuro, Takuro Yoshida and Junichi Inagaki and theme songs for anime series including \"Dragon Ball Z\".\nPage: Shou Tajima. Sentence: Sho-u Tajima (田島 昭宇 , Tajima Shōu ) , born February 7, 1966 in Saitama, Japan, is a manga illustrator and anime character designer.",
